UPDATE companies SET description='QSR Steel Corporation was founded in 2000 in Hartford, Connecticut, as a structural steel and miscellaneous metals fabricator. The company began with a focus on miscellaneous metals before expanding into structural steel in response to customer demand.

The firm operates two AISC‑certified fabrication facilities where it produces structural steel and miscellaneous metal components such as architectural canopies, mezzanines, bollards, ladders, stairs, and railings. In‑house detailing teams use Building Information Modeling (BIM) and CNC‑driven machinery to translate 3D models directly to the shop floor, and the company maintains its own erection crews to handle installation without third‑party subcontractors.

QSR serves construction, renovation, commercial, industrial, retail, education, and municipal clients across New England. Recent projects include the ShopRite supermarket in Cromwell (retail), the Cheney Bennett Pedestrian Bridge in Manchester (commercial/industrial), the William Johnston School (education), and work for the Town of Darien (municipal).

The company emphasizes that controlling both fabrication and erection eliminates coordination delays and quality‑control issues. Its mission cites sustainable procedures certified by AISC, and its track record includes multiple safety awards from the Connecticut Association of Builders and Contractors and recognition as a Top 5000 fastest‑growing company (2008‑2010).', certifications=ARRAY['AISC Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Miscellaneous metals fabrication", "Steel erection", "BIM modeling", "CNC machining", "Computer-aided detailing", "Architectural canopy fabrication", "Mezzanine fabrication", "Bollard fabrication", "Ladder fabrication", "Stair fabrication", "Railing fabrication", "Renovation construction", "Project management", "Estimating"], "industries": ["Construction", "Renovation", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Retail", "Education", "Municipal"], "materials": ["Structural Steel", "Miscellaneous Metals"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AISC\u2011certified structural steel fabrication in two facilities", "In\u2011house fabrication and erection crews", "BIM and CNC\u2011driven production workflow", "Multiple safety awards from the CT Association of Builders and Contractors", "Named a Top 5000 fastest\u2011growing company (2008\u20112010)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 -> /about", "Headquartered in Hartford, CT -> /about", "AISC certified for structural steel fabrication in two facilities -> /services", "In-house fabrication and erection crews -> /services", "BIM and CNC-driven fabrication workflow -> /services", "Projects: Shop Rite in Cromwell, Cheney Bennett Pedestrian Bridge, William Johnston School -> /about", "Safety awards from CT Association of Builders and Contractors -> /", "Top 5000 fastest growing companies 2008-2010 -> /", "Team members: Glenn Salamone (President), Dave Rusconi (VP of Operations), etc. -> /about", "Miscellaneous metals: architectural canopies, mezzanines, bollards, ladders, stairs, rails -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "QSR Steel is an exceptional one-stop, full service structural steel company based in Hartford, CT offering everything from steel buildings to stairs and railings.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='qsr-steel-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Quality Electrical Systems operates from West Jordan, Utah, where it has built a 350,000-square-foot manufacturing facility alongside a 75,000-square-foot inventory warehouse. The company has been in business for three decades, though a specific founding year is not disclosed, and ownership details such as family or veteran status are not publicly stated.

The firm produces custom electrical equipment including switchgear, power distribution centers (PDCs), and variable frequency drives (VFDs). Its OEM manufacturing contracts serve major international brands such as GE/ABB, Yaskawa, Danfoss, and TMEIC. Products ship globally from the Utah campus.

Primary end markets include data centers, oil and gas, water and wastewater treatment, and mining. The company emphasizes design evolution to meet changing industry specifications and customer requirements.

