UPDATE companies SET description='Quabbin Wire & Cable Co Inc operates from Ware, Massachusetts, where it runs two dedicated manufacturing facilities. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year or ownership structure, but it has established itself as a specialist in communication cable design and production.

The company focuses on stranded data cable, harsh‑environment Ethernet, power and control, and multiconductor electronic constructions. One plant is configured exclusively for Ethernet cable production, while the other handles general‑purpose wire and cable. This separation allows operators to optimize each line for efficiency and consistency. Quabbin also offers patch‑cable solutions under its DataMax® brand, including CMP‑rated plenum cables rated to 105 °C, and provides engineering support, cable‑finder tools, and inventory lookup services.

Quabbin’s product lines serve industrial automation, commercial data‑communications, audiovisual and lighting control, and general‑purpose electrical markets. The company’s sales support representatives assist with connector selection and UL certification questions.

Quabbin differentiates itself by holding tighter tolerances than standard requirements and by conducting rigorous testing that exceeds industry norms. It promotes a “USA Made” commitment, 100 % on‑time delivery, competitive pricing, and direct access to cable‑design specialists. The company has been featured on the Discovery Channel, highlighting its manufacturing capabilities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable design and development", "Cable manufacturing", "Stranded data cable production", "Harsh environment Ethernet cable production", "Power and control cable production", "Multiconductor electronic cable production", "Patch cable assembly (DataMax\u00ae)", "Testing and quality assurance", "Engineering support and connector selection assistance", "Inventory management and cable finder tools"], "industries": ["Industrial automation", "Data communications", "Audiovisual and lighting control", "General purpose wire and cable"], "materials": ["Low temperature thermoplastic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Tighter than standard tolerances (specific values not disclosed)", "built_on": ["Two dedicated plants (Ethernet\u2011only and general\u2011purpose)", "Tighter\u2011than\u2011standard manufacturing tolerances", "Testing that surpasses industry requirements", "100\u202f% commitment to on\u2011time delivery and competitive pricing", "In\u2011house cable\u2011design specialists for low\u2011temperature thermoplastic shielded and unshielded cables"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Ware, Massachusetts -> db", "Two dedicated manufacturing plants (one Ethernet-only, one general-purpose) -> /about-us", "Specializes in stranded data cable, harsh environment Ethernet, power and control, multiconductor electronic constructions -> /", "Product categories: Automation and Harsh Environment Data and Control Cable, Commercial Data Cable, Digital AV & Lighting Control Cable, General Purpose Wire & Cable -> /", "Emphasis on tighter tolerances and rigorous testing surpassing industry standards -> /about-us", "USA Made commitment -> /about-us", "UL certification information mentioned -> /about-us", "Featured on Discovery Channel -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At Quabbin, our focus is on manufacturing the best products on the market", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='quabbin-wire-cable-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Quad 4 Plastics operates from Elkhart, Indiana, where it runs two production plants and a distribution warehouse. The company describes itself as a "powerful partner for over 20 years," though a specific founding year is not published. Ownership structure and founders are not disclosed.

The firm provides custom plastic injection molding, thermoforming, and vacuum forming, including insert molding and precision trimming of thermoformed parts. It supports projects from initial sketches through CAD/CAM design, tooling fabrication, and finishing, and adds assembly, packaging, and nationwide distribution from its Elkhart warehouse. The operation specializes in medium- to heavy-gauge thermoplastic parts and emphasizes quick turnarounds.

Quad 4 serves customers in construction furniture, LPG and NH3 equipment, electronics, marine, recreational vehicle, automotive, and general furniture sectors. Its components range from small, complex aesthetic parts to large structural pieces.

